    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;font-size:1.25em;margin-bottom:12px;\">The use of soil to reduce carbon dioxide (CO<sub>2</sub>) in the atmosphere</div><p style=\"font-weight:700;\">Rattan Lal:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Claims that 13% of CO<sub>2</sub> in the atmosphere could be absorbed by agricultural soils</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Erosion is more likely in soil that is <strong>31</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Lai found soil in Africa that was very <strong>32</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; It was suggested that carbon from soil was entering the atmosphere</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Soil and carbon:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; plants turn CO<sub>2</sub> from the air into carbon-based substances such as <strong>33</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; some CO<sub>2</sub> moves from the <strong>34</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> of plants to microbes in the soil</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; carbon was lost from the soil when agriculture was invented</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Regenerative agriculture:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; uses established practices to make sure soil remains fertile and <strong>35</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; e.g. through year-round planting and increasing the <strong>36</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> of plants that are grown</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">California study:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; taking place on a big <strong>37</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> farm</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; uses compost made from waste from agriculture and <strong>38</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Australia study:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; aims to increase soil carbon by using <strong>39</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> that are always green</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Future developments may include:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; reducing the amount of fertilizer used in farming</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; giving farmers <strong>40</strong> <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> for carbon storage, as well as their produce</p></div></div>",
